@cc [owner:tdraier,label:security;mcp] temporal-tools-gated
Every tool handler of the `temporal` MCP server MUST call `enforceTemporalSecurityGates` and return
its `Err` before obtaining a Temporal client or reading any Temporal data.

@cc [owner:tdraier,label:security;mcp] temporal-tools-read-only
Tools of the `temporal` MCP server MUST NOT change Temporal state: no starting, signaling,
updating, canceling, terminating, resetting, pausing, or rescheduling workflows or activities, and
no schedule or task queue changes.
